# Must exist (even before the two real entries below were added) so
# `npm pack`/`publish` doesn't fall back to treating .gitignore as its own
# exclusion list - that would silently drop docs/opencode-docs-reference/
# and deploy/models-dev-snapshot.json, both gitignored-but-git-tracked on
# purpose (see CLAUDE.md) and both things the offline target machine
# actually needs.
#
# The two entries below exclude mcp-servers/java-lsp's and
# mcp-servers/spring-lsp's own vendored jdtls/spring-boot-language-server
# tarballs (~51MB/~81MB) from THIS root package specifically - installing
# either MCP server always goes through its own separately-published
# @kealthas-dev/opencode-mcp-java-lsp/-spring-lsp package (which whitelists
# vendor/*.tar.gz in its own package.json "files" field), never through the
# root package, so carrying a second copy of either tarball here is pure
# waste. This stopped being cosmetic 2026-09-24: once vendor/ at the repo
# root also started carrying the ~200MB split JDK (see CLAUDE.md's `vendor/`
# row), the root package's total size tripped npm's own publish payload
# limit (real failure: 333.5MB packed -> 413 Payload Too Large) - trimming
# this redundant ~132MB is what brings it back under.
mcp-servers/java-lsp/vendor/
mcp-servers/spring-lsp/vendor/
